// The most common fragment shader there is: one constant colour
// (t_642eb36e).
//
// Reference compiler:
//
//     FENCBR;
//     MOVR R0, {0x3f800000(1), 0, 0, 0}.x;
//
// One value in the block, broadcast by the swizzle.  Ours wrote
// 0x3f800000 four times with an identity swizzle until 2026-09-02, which
// is the same picture and a different container - and this is the shape
// the rig's own generated coverage shaders use, so the byte fence saw it
// before any corpus shader did.
void main(out float4 oColor : COLOR)
{
    oColor = float4(1.0f, 1.0f, 1.0f, 1.0f);
}
